<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-linearequations" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Solving Linear Equations</title>

<p>A linear function equation is one that can be written in the form <m>ax=b</m>. They may not always be presented
in this form though. </p>

<p>To solve a linear equation we want to isolate the variable <m>x</m>.Any operation performed on one side
  of the equation must also be performed on the other side. From the form <m>ax=b</m>, we can isolate <m>x</m> by 
dividing both sides of the equation by <m>a</m>. </p>

<example>
    <title>Solving Equations of the Form <m>ax=b</m></title>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Solve the equation <m>5x=45</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p> We divide both sides of the equation by 5. On the left, dividing by 5 leaves only <m>x</m>. On the right, 
        dividing by 5 gives 9. Then the resulting equation reads <m>x=9</m>.
      </p>
    </solution>
  </example>

  <p>If the linear equation is given in a more complex form, we apply the following general steps:</p>
  <p>
<ol>
<li>
Expand any brackets.
</li>
<li>
Group all terms involving <m>x</m> on one side of the equation, and all constant terms on the other side.
</li>
<li>
Simplify each side to give the form <m>ax=b</m>.
</li>
<li>
Divide both sides of the equation by <m>a</m>.
</li>
</ol>
</p>

<example>
    <title>Solving Linear Equations</title>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Solve the equation <m>3(x-2)+1=3+x</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p> We first expand the brackets by multiplying each term inside by 3,</p>
      <md>3(x-2)=3x-3(2)=3x-6.</md>
      <p>We then shift all terms involving <m>x</m> to the left-hand-side of the equation, and all constant
      terms to the right-hand-side. In this case, there is an <m>x</m> term on the right-hand-side, so we 
      subtract <m>x</m> from both sides. The left-hand-side has terms -6 and +1, so we add 6 and subtract 1 from
      both sides.</p>
      <md>3x-6+1=3+x</md>
      <md>3x-6+1-x+6-1=3+x-x+6-1</md>
      <md>3x-x=3+6-1</md>
      <p>Simplifying each side gives</p>
      <md>2x=8.</md>
      <p>We can now divide by 2 to obtain the result <m>x=4</m>.</p>
    </solution>
  </example>

  <exercise label="ww-linear">
    <title>Solving Linear Equations</title>
    <webwork>
        <pg-code>
            # Set the math environment to expect fraction format answers
            Context("Fraction-NoDecimals");
            
            # Define the exact answer
            $x = 7;
        </pg-code>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Solve the equation <m>4-2x=3(5-x)-4</m>.
            </p>   
            <p><m>x=</m><var name="$x" width="10"/>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </webwork>
</exercise>

<subsection>
  <title>Exercises</title>


<exercise label="ww-linear2">
    <webwork>
        <pg-code>
            # Set the math environment to expect fraction format answers
            Context("Fraction-NoDecimals");
            
            # Define the exact answer
            $x = -3;
        </pg-code>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Solve the equation <m>3-4x=3(x+8)</m>.
            </p>   
            <p><m>x=</m><var name="$x" width="10"/>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </webwork>
</exercise>

<exercise label="ww-linear3">
    <webwork>
        <pg-code>
            # Set the math environment to expect fraction format answers
            Context("Fraction-NoDecimals");
            
            # Define the exact answer
            $x = 4;
        </pg-code>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Solve the equation <m>5(x+2)-10=4(x+1)</m>.
            </p>   
            <p><m>x=</m><var name="$x" width="10"/>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </webwork>
</exercise>

<exercise label="ww-linear4">
    <webwork>
        <pg-code>
            # Set the math environment to expect fraction format answers
            Context("Fraction-NoDecimals");
            
            # Define the exact answer
            $x = -2;
        </pg-code>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Solve the equation <m>2-4(5-x)=5(x-3)-1</m>.
            </p>   
            <p><m>x=</m><var name="$x" width="10"/>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </webwork>
</exercise>




</subsection>

</section>